        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED &amp; PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: LOW LHS BLEED PRESSURE DUING ALL STAGES OF THE FLIGHT. SUSPECTED FAULTY SENSE LINE. BAR AND PRSOV ALREADY REPLACED.

ACTION:  
 
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS.  
 
2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
 
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
 
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
 
3. INSPECT ALL SYSTEM SENSE LINES AND CONNECTIONS FOR ANY SIGNS OF DAMAGE, BLOCKAGE OR LEAKAGE. MAKE THE NECESSARY RECTIFICATIONS.
  
4. MANUALLY WRENCH PRSOV USING APU BLEED SOURCE AND LEAK CHECK TO ALL SENSE LINES.
 
5. LEAK CHECK TO ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE OR FITTINGS AND SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR PN 115347.
 
6. DISCONNECT 390 SENSE LINE FROM PCCV UNION AND 390 SENSOR, USING COMPRESSED NITROGEN BLOW OUT SENSE LINE AND RECORD IF ANY BLOCKAGE IS FOUND. CHECK PCCV UNION FOR OBSTRUCTION THAT MAY ALSO RESTRICT VENTING PCCV CONTROL PRESSURE.

7. CLOSELY INSPECT LH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.
 
8. CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.
 
9. REPLACE ANY FAULTY COMPONENT FOUND IAW AMM.
 
10. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.   
 
**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  
 
**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
